quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  2,253,"Those are the Messengers—We have honoured some above others. Among them is the one to whom Allah spoke (directly), and He raised some of them in ranks. And We gave ‘Isa (Jesus), the son of Maryam (Mary), clear signs and strengthened him with the Holy Spirit. Had Allah willed, those who succeeded them would not have fought one another after the clear proofs had come to them. But they differed (between themselves): among them were some who believed, and among them were others who disbelieved. Had Allah willed, they would not have fought (among themselves). However, Allah does whatever He wills."
  2,254,"O believers! Spend from what we have provided you before a day arrives when there shall be neither trading, nor friendship, nor intercession. And the disbelievers—they are the wrongdoers."
  2,255,"Allah! There is no god except Him, the Ever-Living, the All-Sustainer. Neither drowsiness nor sleep overtakes Him. To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. Who can intercede with Him except by His permission? He knows what is before them and what is behind them. They cannot comprehend anything of His knowledge except what He wills. His Throne extends over the heavens and the earth, and it does not tire Him to preserve them both. He is the All-Exalted, the All-Supreme."
  2,256,"There is no compulsion in religion. True guidance has become distinct from error. So, the one who renounces false gods and believes in Allah has grasped the firmest handhold. It is not breakable, and Allah is All-Hearing, All-Knowing."
